#import "../../../proofs.typ": speech, footnote

== 24. Of The Civil Magistrate

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 1]: God, the supreme Lord and King of all the world, hath ordained civil magistrates to be under Him, over the people, for His own glory and the public good; and to this end has armed them with the power of the sword, for defence and encouragement of them that do good, and for the punishment of evil doers.#footnote[Romans 13:1–4]]

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 2]: It is lawful for Christians to accept and execute the office of a magistrate when called thereunto; in the management whereof, as they ought especially to maintain justice and peace,#footnote[2 Samuel 23:3; Psalm 82:3–4] according to the wholesome laws of each kingdom and commonwealth, so for that end they may lawfully now, under the New Testament, wage war upon just and necessary occasions.#footnote[Luke 3:14]]

#speech[#smallcaps[Paragraph 3]: Civil magistrates being set up by God for the ends aforesaid; subjection, in all lawful things commanded by them, ought to be yielded by us in the Lord, not only for wrath, but for conscience’ sake;#footnote[Romans 13:5–7; 1 Peter 2:17] and we ought to make supplications and prayers for kings and all that are in authority, that under them we may live a quiet and peaceable life, in all godliness and honesty.#footnote[1 Timothy 2:1–2]]
